  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#342)
    notes: 'mapping_quality NARROW_MATCH -> CLOSE_MATCH, predicate skos:narrowMatch
      -> skos:closeMatch. narrowMatch asserts this record is *narrower in meaning*
      than CHEBI:17285 (''L-cysteic acid'') — a subsumption ChEBI itself denies: it
      files hydrates under CHEBI:35505 ''hydrate'', never under the anhydrous compound,
      which is not an ancestor even transitively. A hydrate is a distinct substance
      containing the anhydrous form, not a specialization of it. closeMatch claims
      similarity without subsumption. The ontology_id and the record''s own identifier
      are unchanged.'
  - evidence_type: MANUAL_CURATION
    source: MIM Step7d scientific review (#901)
    notes: 'Catalogueline1338 CAS23537-25-9/FW187.17 and PubChemCID12308854 establish
      L-cysteic acid monohydrate, including the L-specific stereochemical InChI. CHEBI17285
      is L-cysteicacid without water. No exacthydrate candidate found; retainCAS and
      broadMatch plus separate B1registry. See the complete identity, mapping, chemistry
      and synonym assessment in reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/authors/science-b/full-assessments.json;
      owner selector data/ingredients/mapped/L-Cysteic_Acid_Monohydrate.yaml. Primary
      source references: https://github.com/CultureBotAI/CultureBotHT; https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/rest/pug/compound/name/23537-25-9/property/MolecularFormula,MolecularWeight,InChI,InChIKey,IUPACName/JSON;
      https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/backend/api/public/compound/17285/. Captures, exact
      input hashes and scope limits: reports/step7d_mapping_901_20261103/evidence-manifest.json.
      This curation adds no scientific, mapping-release or role approval; changed
      owner bytes withdraw inherited support.'
